{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For He says to the snow</b> — \"to be on the earth.\" And I have already mentioned in the book Moznayim ha-Lashon that every thing requires time and place; therefore there are instances in the sacred language without the letter bet, such as: \"Is the house of YHWH found?\" [translating הנמצא בית ה' as if the bet of place is absent]."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {0 "The example הנמצא בית ה' is hyper-literal as Ibn Ezra quotes it; he is illustrating that בית can appear without a prefixed bet meaning 'in', yet still carry locative force. The exact biblical source of this phrase is uncertain; it may be a loose citation or paraphrase rather than a verbatim verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:51.272458546Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}